{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking","lean:module:QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel","lean:module:QOU.Mass.MilnorIndeterminacyGate"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation.clusterTriple_brunnian_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation.clusterTriple_brunnian_iff","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTierDisambiguation.lean#L111-L115","doc":"**T2 in its concrete `ClusterTriple` form is the same condition.**  Recorded\nso a reader holding a `ClusterTriple` can reach the pointwise form without\nre-deriving the translation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation.signed_zero_but_energy_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation.signed_zero_but_energy_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTierDisambiguation.lean#L101-L109","doc":"**And the two channels genuinely disagree on such a pair**: the signed\nchannel is zero while the total is not.  So \"the linking number vanishes\" and\n\"the mutual energy vanishes\" are not two readings of one fact — they differ on\nexactly the configurations this framework's carriers are made of. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation.noIsolatedPairEnergy_fails_for_crossing_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation.noIsolatedPairEnergy_fails_for_crossing_pair","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTierDisambiguation.lean#L85-L99","doc":"**T4 fails for every crossing pair — the statement that was walked past.**\n\nA pair with `n₊ = n₋ = m` and `0 < m` has vanishing linking number (so T2 and T3\nhold of it) and **strictly positive** mutual energy, so `NoIsolatedPairEnergy`\n(`w₂ = 0`) is false of it.  Vanishing linking does not empty the energy; it\nempties only the *signed* channel, and the unsigned count channel survives.\n\nRestated from `brunnian_binding_survives` under the name of the property it\nrefutes, because the failure mode this file exists to prevent was reading a\ntheorem about linking as a theorem about energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation.linkingVanishes_iff_forall_at","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation.linkingVanishes_iff_forall_at","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BrunnianTierDisambiguation.lean#L66-L83","doc":"**T2 ⟺ T3, on a three-component cluster.**\n\nAll three pairwise linking numbers vanish exactly when every component is\nunlinked from the other two.  Symmetry of the linking matrix is a hypothesis\nbecause `BrunnianAt` reads the matrix in one direction only; the Gauss linking\nnumber is symmetric, so this is not a restriction in practice.\n\nThis is the bridge `MilnorIndeterminacyGate` and\n`FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking` never had between them — they state\nthe same condition, one globally and one pointwise, and nothing related them. ","signatureChunk":0}]}